    What legitimate right do you think is infringed upon in such cases.

Life.  Exposing someone to a disease is an initiation of physical
aggression, and should be actionable according to normal tort and
criminal standards as to intent, severity, and mitigating factors.

Think about the equivalent situation of someone with a vial 
containing a biotoxin.  They have a responsibility to take 
precautions to prevent accidental exposure proportionate to the
harm caused by such exposure.

As to mitigating factors, I had an interesting thought:  there is a
legal maxim that a plaintiff must have done everything they reasonably
could to reduce the impact of the defendant's actions.  If they did
not, the award/punishment can be less or nothing, depending on the two
parties' relative contributions to the consequences of the act.

So if I infect you, and you sue me, I can argue that the primary
reason you got sick is because of your poor immune response,
brought on by not enough vitamin C, too much sugar, smoking, etc.

